                <invention-title lang="de">VERFAHREN UND VORRICHTUNGEN FÜR HIGH-LEVEL-SYNTAX IN DER VIDEOCODIERUNG</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">PROCÉDÉS ET DISPOSITIFS POUR SYNTAXE DE HAUT NIVEAU DANS UN CODAGE VIDÉO</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">METHODS AND DEVICES FOR HIGH-LEVEL SYNTAX IN VIDEO CODING</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Methods, devices, and storage mediums are provided for decoding video signals. A method for decoding a video signal, comprising: receiving, by a decoder, inter prediction related syntax elements in sequence parameter set (SPS) level, wherein the inter prediction related syntax elements are sequentially arranged at a coding level, and wherein the inter prediction related syntax elements comprise an sps_weighted_pred_flag flag, an sps_weighted_bipred_flag flag, an sps_mmvd_enabled_flag flag, a six_minus _max_num_merge_cand syntax element, and a log2_parallel_merge_level_minus2 syntax element, the sps _weighted_pred_flag flag equal to 1 specifies that weighted prediction might be applied to P slices referring to SPS, the sps _weighted_pred_flag flag equal to 0 specifies that weighted prediction is not applied to P slices referring to SPS, the sps_weighted_bipred_flag flag equal to 1 specifies that explicit weighted prediction might be applied to B slices referring to SPS, the sps_weighted_bipred_flag flag equal to 0 specifies that explicit weighted prediction is not applied to B slices referring to SPS, the sps_mmvd_enabled_flag flag equal to 1 specifies that merge mode with motion vector difference is enabled, the sps_mmvd_enabled_flag flag equal to 0 specifies that merge mode with motion vector difference is disabled, the six_minus_max_num_merge_cand syntax element specifies a maximum number of merging motion vector prediction candidates supported in SPS subtracted from 6, the log2_parallel_merge_level_minus2 syntax element plus 2 specifies a value of a variable Log2ParMrgLevel, which is used in at least one of a derivation process for spatial merging candidates, a derivation process for motion vectors and reference indices in subblock merge mode, and controlling of invocation of an updating process for history-based motion vector predictor list, and wherein the inter prediction related syntax elements are arranged by: signaling the sps _weighted_pred_flag flag, signaling the sps_weighted_bipred_flag flag, signaling the sps _mmvd_enabled_flag flag, setting a value of the six_minus_max_num_merge_cand syntax element, and setting a value of the log2_parallel_merge_level_minus2 syntax element; obtaining, by the decoder, first prediction samples of a video block from a first reference picture associated with the video block; obtaining, by the decoder, second prediction samples of the video block from a second reference picture associated with the video block, wherein the second reference picture is different from the first reference picture; and obtaining, by the decoder, bi-prediction samples based on at least one of the inter prediction related syntax elements, the first prediction samples, and the second prediction samples, wherein the method further comprises receiving an sps_isp_enabled_flag flag after the log2_parallel_merge_level_minus2 syntax element, the sps_isp_enabled_flag flag equal to 1 specifies that intra prediction with subpartitions is enabled, the sps _isp_enabled_flag flag equal to 0 specifies that intra prediction with subpartitions is disabled.</p>
            </abstract>
